#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/fa.rc -- Persian (Iran), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "fa"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. Right to left: no direction marks anywhere in the strings, the
// window is mirrored by the code. The arrow of the cycle and the separator of a list are the
// language's own (IDS_CYCLE_ARROW, IDS_LIST_SEPARATOR); the stand checks them. Quotes are the
// guillemets «», the full stop is the Latin ".", the comma «،», the semicolon «؛», the question
// mark «؟». Persian letters only: KEHEH U+06A9 and FARSI YEH U+06CC, never the Arabic KAF and YEH;
// the half-space (ZWNJ, U+200C) stands where the norm of the language needs it (the prefix «می»,
// the plural «ها», the suffix «ی» after a silent «ه»).
// Keys stay in Latin letters as the program prints them. Where each string is seen and how much
// room it has is res/lang/context.tsv; the terms are in l10n/glossary/fa.tsv.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Persian — `[general] language = "fa"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
